<article class="env-lemma" id="0ETG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ETG">Lemma <span data-tag="0ETG">34.10.6</span>.</a> Let $T$ be an affine scheme. Let $\{ T_ j \to T\} _{j = 1, \ldots , m}$ be a family of morphisms with $T_ j$ affine for all $j$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\{ T_ j \to T\} _{j = 1, \ldots , m}$ is a standard V covering, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there is a standard V covering which refines $\{ T_ j \to T\} _{j = 1, \ldots , m}$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\{ \coprod _{j = 1, \ldots , m} T_ j \to T\} $ is a standard V covering. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hints: This follows almost immediately from the definition. The only slightly interesting point is that a morphism from the spectrum of a local ring into $\coprod _{j = 1, \ldots , m} T_ j$ must factor through some $T_ j$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>